      "id": 1,
      "text": "Wanakena was founded in 1902 by cousins Herbert and Horace Rich, who started the Rich Brothers Lumber Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wanakena%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A logging railroad linked Wanakena to the Carthage and Adirondack Railroad in 1905, fueling the mill town’s growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wanakena%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic footbridge, listed on the National Register in 1999, was lost to an ice jam in January 2014.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
